  [ceiling · answered] The suction-chain, discharge-chain and fluid-14 tunnel roofs are the backs of the clamping ribs: the zip tie passes under each rib and pulls its body into the seat. Each roof bridges 2.8 mm along X between complete 3 mm feet; the 23.3 mm or 12.7 mm transverse extent is the rib's width. The recessed floor provides 3.25 mm of clear height. The cleanout lane runs along Y through either open mouth, before the purchased body and tie are fitted. Release any attached support at its contact faces and clear the 0.25 mm floor-relief lip before withdrawing it through a mouth; the relief is not a flush floor-level slide path.
